# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets _headers starter template.
# Copy/adapt to the deployed site's public/_headers or configured build output.
# Confirm the actual Worker assets directory before deployment.

 /*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.example.com; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000

# Optional: apply stronger caching to fingerprinted static assets after confirming
# the Angular build emits content-hashed filenames.
# /assets/*
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# IMPORTANT:
# - Replace https://api.example.com with the exact API origins actually used.
# - HSTS max-age=31536000 is appropriate only after HTTPS is reliable on every
#   affected hostname. Add includeSubDomains only if every subdomain supports HTTPS.
# - Do not add preload casually; it has long-lived operational consequences.
# - 'unsafe-inline' in style-src is a compatibility compromise some Angular/UI
#   setups need. Test whether it can be removed or replaced with hashes/nonces.
# - script-src 'self' may need adjustment for SSR, inline bootstrap code, analytics,
#   or other integrations. Prefer hashes/nonces over 'unsafe-inline'.
# - CSP is application-specific. Test in report-only mode first where practical,
#   inspect violations, then enforce. Do not blindly deploy this policy.
# - X-Frame-Options is retained for compatibility; frame-ancestors is the modern
#   CSP control. Adjust both if legitimate framing is required.
